package viewslegal

import "whatsappconverty/internal/i18n"

// DataDeletion is the public data-deletion instructions page. Meta's app
// review asks for a Data Deletion Instructions URL whenever an app stores user
// data, so it is served unauthenticated at /data-deletion and describes exactly
// what the Platform holds, how to ask for erasure and what is retained. The
// chrome follows the viewer's language; the legal text stays in English.
templ DataDeletion(supportEmail string, dict *i18n.Dict) {
	@Shell("Data Deletion Instructions", "How to request deletion of your personal data held by Converty WhatsApp.", dict) {
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Data Deletion Instructions</h1>
		<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: September 27, 2026</p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
			This page explains what personal data Converty WhatsApp (the "Platform") holds, how
			to ask us to delete it, and what we are required to keep. It is the companion to
			our <a href="/privacy" class="font-medium text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">Privacy Policy</a>.
		</p>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
			<section>
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">1. What data we hold</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">For your shop we hold:</p>
				<ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
					<li><span class="font-medium">Account data</span> — your name, email address and a hashed password, plus active sign-in sessions.</li>
					<li><span class="font-medium">Integration data</span> — your shop details, the Converty and WhatsApp credentials you connected (stored encrypted), your WhatsApp number and business account identifiers.</li>
					<li><span class="font-medium">Automation configuration</span> — the order statuses you chose to notify, the templates you selected, the send times you set and the tokens each template fills in.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-2">For your customers we hold:</p>
				<ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
					<li><span class="font-medium">Customer records</span> — the name and phone number of a customer who received a message from you, and their consent or opt-out status.</li>
					<li><span class="font-medium">Message records</span> — what was sent, to which number, using which template, with its delivery status and timestamps.</li>
					<li><span class="font-medium">Order and delivery records</span> — the order references, statuses, tracking codes, carrier and driver details needed to produce your notifications, and the last time each parcel was polled.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">2. How to request deletion</h2>
				@contactLine(supportEmail, "Data deletion request", dict)
				<p class="mt-2">
					If you are a customer of one of the shops using the Platform, the fastest route is
					to ask that shop directly, since it decides which messages you receive. You can
					also write to us directly and we will pass the request to the relevant shop.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2">
					We aim to confirm receipt within 7 days and to complete the deletion within 30
					days of confirming the request. We will tell you what we deleted and what, if
					anything, we are required to retain.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">3. What we delete</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					On request we remove your account and integration credentials, your automation
					configuration, and the customer, consent, message, order and delivery records
					associated with your shop. We also stop all sending immediately: a deletion
					request is treated as a full opt-out, so no further message can be sent to the
					affected numbers.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">4. What we keep, and why</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Some records are retained in a reduced or anonymised form where we are required
					or permitted to keep them:
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
					<li><span class="font-medium">Message delivery evidence</span> — we keep the fact that a message was sent and its delivery status, without the message body, for the period needed to answer delivery disputes and billing enquiries.</li>
					<li><span class="font-medium">Suppression records</span> — we keep a record of numbers that asked not to be contacted, so we never re-send to someone who opted out. Deleting these would let us contact a recipient again by mistake.</li>
					<li><span class="font-medium">Security and operational logs</span> — retained to investigate abuse, fraud and incidents, and then deleted.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">5. Data held by other providers</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Messages are delivered through Meta's WhatsApp Business infrastructure, and a
					copy of the message content, recipient number and delivery status is processed by
					Meta under its own policies and retention rules. We cannot erase data from
					Meta's systems on your behalf. We can, and do, stop sending to a number and
					delete our own copy of your data. Converty and the carrier share only the
					details listed in section 1 of this page, and you can ask us to stop the
					corresponding integration, which ends that sharing.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">6. Contact</h2>
				<p class="mt-2">
					Questions about this page, or about the deletion of your data, can be sent to
					our support team.
				</p>
				@contactLine(supportEmail, "Data deletion request", dict)
			</section>
		</div>

		@legalFooter(dict)
	}
}
